type: software
title: "Система оценки качества ответов больших языковых моделей по новостным текстам стран Восточной Азии"
abstract: >-
  Bachelor's thesis repository (Faculty of Computational Mathematics and Cybernetics, Lomonosov
  Moscow State University). Systems in which a large language model answers questions about
  articles in a news archive are being deployed faster than ways to check their answers appear.
  Existing test sets are in English or contain questions whose answers change over time, and the
  agreement of automatic evaluation with humans and of annotators with each other is usually not
  reported. This thesis builds a system for evaluating answers to questions about East Asian
  news: the question is asked in Russian, and the sources are written in Chinese. What is
  evaluated is the answer, that is, the text and the cited documents. The evaluation system has
  four parts. First, a rigorous problem statement restricted to questions whose answers do not
  change over time, so that the reference does not go stale. Second, a reference set of
  questions with answers and supporting documents, including questions whose correct answer is
  "I don't know"; each question is annotated independently by three people, and their agreement
  is measured. Third, metrics of correctness, citation accuracy, abstention and retrieval;
  correctness and citation scores, including those produced by another language model, are
  admitted to the comparison only if they agree with human ratings on Russian-language answers.
  Fourth, a paired statistical test of differences between systems on the same questions with a
  correction for multiple comparisons. The object of study is the industrial system "Chinese
  Media Analysis" of the Institute of Oriental Studies of the Russian Academy of Sciences (an
  archive of 23.9 million chunks). It is to be compared with six open models without retrieval
  and over the same retrieval results, 13 systems in total.
